    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d479">

                <pb facs="0655" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1934v03/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/6625: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-05-07T18:00:00-04:00">May 7, 1934—6 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Please inform Canton in reference to its telegram of April 29, noon,<anchor
                        n="24" xml:id="d479-f1"/> as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>In your discretion, you are authorized, on some opportune occasion when
                            you are discussing with members of the Southwest Political Council and
                            other officials at Canton the oil discrimination matter or <pb
                                facs="0656" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/> other cases of discriminatory
                            treatment of Americans at Canton, to refer to the declaration made by
                            the Southwest Political Council on April 27 and to remind them of their
                            obligation to observe treaties between China and the foreign powers.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
